<!--
    Plain Microsoft.NET.Sdk, NOT Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web, even though this project serves HTTP.
    Do not switch this back.

    WHY. The Web SDK is for applications; this is a packable class library that happens to carry
    API controllers and an embedded SPA. Using it pulled in the Razor SDK, which feeds
    Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.Razor.Compiler.dll to the compiler as an analyzer — for a project with
    zero .razor/.cshtml files. On .NET SDK 10.0.400 that analyzer requires Roslyn 5.9, which the
    Metalama Compiler arriving transitively (Vion.Dale.DevHost -> Vion.Dale.Sdk) does not supply,
    so every build in the repo failed with LAMA0625. Bumping Metalama does not fix it: the newest
    release (2026.1.23) still bundles Roslyn 5.6.

    ASP.NET Core types come from the FrameworkReference below — the documented way for a *library*
    to compile against them. Controllers are still discovered normally (ApplicationPart at runtime;
    the SDK type is irrelevant to that).

    TWO CONSEQUENCES, both verified.

    1. The package no longer carries staticwebassets/ (nor the build/*.props that wire them up).
       That is dead weight removed, not a regression: WebHostService serves the SPA exclusively
       through EmbeddedFileProvider over the EmbeddedResource below — UseDefaultFiles,
       UseStaticFiles and MapFallbackToFile each pass that provider explicitly. The Web SDK was
       shipping every SPA file a second time; the .nupkg went 823 KB -> 426 KB.
    2. Microsoft.AspNetCore.Analyzers and Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Analyzers are no longer applied
       here — they are contributed by the Web SDK, not by the FrameworkReference. That is a real
       (small) loss of MVC/routing diagnostics over this project's few controllers, accepted
       because the alternative is a repo-wide broken build.
-->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
        <ImplicitUsings>false</ImplicitUsings>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <OutputType>Library</OutputType>

        <!-- NuGet package metadata -->
        <PackageId>Vion.Dale.DevHost.Web</PackageId>
        <Description>Dale DevHost Web UI for local development and testing</Description>
        <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <!-- ASP.NET Core surface for a library: the Web SDK would imply this, plain Sdk does not. -->
        <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App"/>
    </ItemGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <!-- Embed the SPA build output. Under the Web SDK, wwwroot/** was ALSO implicitly Content;
             under plain Sdk it is only what this line says, which is what the runtime reads
             (EmbeddedFileProvider in WebHostService). -->
        <EmbeddedResource Include="wwwroot\**\*"/>
    </ItemGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\Vion.Dale.DevHost\Vion.Dale.DevHost.csproj"/>
    </ItemGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <Folder Include="wwwroot\"/>
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>